s after Chi would be too scattered (W1-W2, W9-W9, B4-B6-B8) with poor winning chances; (2) I already have one exposed meld, so maintaining some concealment helps preserve scoring options; (3) The B5 doesn't significantly improve my hand structure enough to justify the commitment; (4) Keeping flexibility allows me to adapt to future draws.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
