It's unlikely to be claimed by others based on game history\n- Keeps my options open for Half Flush pattern\n\nReason: \nW9 is a terminal tile that doesn't contribute to any potential winning pattern in my hand. I'm developing a Dots-suit concentration with potential for Half Flush (6 points). Keeping W1 and W2 provides minimal flexibility, but W9 duplicate is the least useful. The next player has already shown no interest in W9, making it a safe discard.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
